~ start
Prime Minister Zawadzki: You should know that in Silesia a French president is either a guest or a bailiff. Tonight you are a guest. Keep it that way.
- Offer a just-transition fund => transition
- Offer a French nuclear partnership => nuclear
- Offer to defend Poland's pace at the council => pace
~ transition
Prime Minister Zawadzki: A just-transition fund. The miners' union has heard the word before, and still it is a good word to hear from a visitor.
- Fund it from the French budget => french_budget
- Fund it from a European line => european_line
~ french_budget
Prime Minister Zawadzki: From Paris? The miners will drink to you. My finance minister will check the cheque twice.
=> END
~ european_line
Prime Minister Zawadzki: A European line is a longer wait, but nobody here will say I took French money to close a mine.
=> END
~ nuclear
Prime Minister Zawadzki: Nuclear is the future in the cities and the past in the villages. We will build, but you will not decide where.
- Offer reactor technology => reactor
- Offer only training and expertise => training
~ reactor
Prime Minister Zawadzki: Reactors. We will argue about the site, the cost, and the fuel. But we will build.
=> END
~ training
Prime Minister Zawadzki: Training. Cheap, honest, and eventually necessary. I accept.
=> END
~ pace
Prime Minister Zawadzki: Poland's pace is its own. Brussels dictates the year, we negotiate the decade, and the miners keep the lamp.
- Say the pace should be Poland's => poland_pace
- Say the pace should be Europe's => europe_pace
~ poland_pace
Prime Minister Zawadzki: A friend. In Warsaw we remember who says what to which crowd.
=> END
~ europe_pace
Prime Minister Zawadzki: Europe's pace. Well. At least you said it to my face.
=> END
